# Run the API (dotnet run --project samples/Shop.Api) and send these one by one from Rider, VS or VS Code.
@api = http://localhost:5080

### 1. The warehouse receives 5 keyboards
POST {{api}}/stock/KEYBOARD
Content-Type: application/json

{ "quantity": 5 }

### 2. A customer places an order -> 202 Accepted
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "A-1001", "sku": "KEYBOARD", "quantity": 1, "amount": 89 }

### 3. The orders screen: A-1001 is Paid, waiting for the payment provider
GET {{api}}/orders

### 4. The payment provider confirms -> the order ships
POST {{api}}/webhooks/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "A-1001" }

### 5. The order, with its process status
GET {{api}}/orders/A-1001

### 6. Double click on "Buy" -> 409 AlreadyPlaced
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "A-1001", "sku": "KEYBOARD", "quantity": 1, "amount": 89 }

### 7. Card declined (over 1000) -> stock released, order Cancelled
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "A-1002", "sku": "KEYBOARD", "quantity": 1, "amount": 2500 }

### 8. Make the payment gateway flaky, then order: watch the retries in the journal (1s, 2s)
POST {{api}}/dev/payment-gateway/fail?times=2

###
POST {{api}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "A-1003", "sku": "KEYBOARD", "quantity": 1, "amount": 50 }

### 9. Nobody confirms A-1003: jump 15 minutes ahead -> timeout, refund, release
POST {{api}}/dev/clock/advance?minutes=15

### 10. Stock is consistent: 5 received - 1 shipped = 4
GET {{api}}/stock/KEYBOARD

### What happened, step by step
GET {{api}}/dev/journal

### Integration events other services would receive
GET {{api}}/dev/published
